    <main id="ds-main" class="ds-page">
      <!-- =========================== HERO =============================== -->
      <header class="ds-hero">
        <nav class="cer-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">shupp.dev</a>
          <svg class="icon icon--xs icon--mark" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron-right" /></svg>
          <a href="/portfolio">Design</a>
          <svg class="icon icon--xs icon--mark" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron-right" /></svg>
          <span aria-current="page">Ceramic</span>
        </nav>

        <p class="cer-eyebrow">CERAMIC · v1.0 · BOUNDARY DEPTH</p>
        <h1 class="cer-display">Ceramic</h1>
        <span class="ds-aside">Depth lives at the edge of a thing, never inside it.</span>
        <p class="cer-text ds-intro">
          A dark, single-mode system built on one perceptual trick. Every object is
          drawn with a 1.5px hairline of absolute black; a hard, short light gradient
          sits immediately inside it and a soft, long dark one immediately outside.
          The asymmetry drives lateral inhibition harder than a real edge would, so a
          face that is one flat colour edge to edge reads as glazed, lifted material.
          Two objects filled with the same hex can be two different substances.
          Press <span style="color: var(--ink)">Strip the pair</span> above to take the
          gradients away and watch the page fall flat — the fill never changes.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- ========================= 1 · BOUNDARY ========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-boundary">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">INVARIANTS I1–I3 · THE BOUNDARY</p>
          <h2 id="ds-boundary" class="cer-h2">One hairline, two unequal gradients</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            The mechanism is the Cornsweet illusion. All three discs below are filled
            with exactly <code>#1c1e26</code> — sample the centre of each with a colour
            picker and you get the same value. Only the twelve pixels either side of
            their edge differ.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-ab">
          <div class="ds-spec">
            <div class="ds-slab ds-bare"></div>
            <p class="ds-cap">hairline alone<br /><span class="ds-swatch-hex">#1c1e26</span></p>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-spec">
            <div class="ds-slab lit lit--sz-sm"></div>
            <p class="ds-cap">.lit — pair + decay<br /><span class="ds-swatch-hex">#1c1e26</span></p>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-spec">
            <div class="ds-slab lit lit--ceramic"></div>
            <p class="ds-cap">.lit--ceramic — decay 0<br /><span class="ds-swatch-hex">#1c1e26</span></p>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-spec">
            <div class="ds-slab lit lit--sunk"></div>
            <p class="ds-cap">.lit--sunk — pair inverted<br /><span class="ds-swatch-hex">#16181f</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cer-card lit" style="margin-top: 22px">
          <div class="ds-rule">
            <span class="n">I1</span>
            <p><b>The hairline is #000000, 1.5px, always</b>On every object, at every size. It never scales, never takes a colour, never becomes a border-width token. It is a boundary marker, not a stroke weight.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-rule">
            <span class="n">I2</span>
            <p><b>The page is never black</b>Absolute black has to be darker than its surround, or the hairline stops reading as a void and starts reading as fill. The page floor is <code>--s0</code>, #101118.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-rule">
            <span class="n">I3</span>
            <p><b>The pair is asymmetric</b>Inside: hard and short — 1.5px offset, zero blur. Outside: soft and long — 7 to 9px offset, 12 to 16px blur. Symmetric decay cancels the illusion and leaves you with something merely blurry.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-rule">
            <span class="n">I6</span>
            <p><b>Fills are flat</b>A component has one background value. All variation lives in <code>box-shadow</code>. There is no gradient anywhere in this system that is not a shadow.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================= 2 · SURFACES ========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-surfaces">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§3 · SURFACE LADDER</p>
          <h2 id="ds-surfaces" class="cer-h2">Four values, lightest object on darkest page</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            Each step is roughly +6 per channel. Four surfaces is the whole ladder — a
            design that appears to need a fifth needs a different depth preset instead.
            Status hues sit at low chroma deliberately: a 1.5px band at 42% alpha against
            <code>--s2</code> is already near the perceptual limit, and saturated hue
            blooms on near-black panels. To make a state clearer, raise
            <code>--lift</code>, never the saturation.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--4">
          {surfaces.map((s) => (
            <div class="ds-surface lit lit--ceramic" style={`background: ${s.hex}`}>
              <span class="nm">{s.name} · {s.hex}</span>
              <span class="rl">{s.role}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================== 3 · DEPTH =========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-depth">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§4 · THE DEPTH PRIMITIVE</p>
          <h2 id="ds-depth" class="cer-h2">Three presets over one shadow structure</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            Material light is directional and always white (I4) — it describes what an
            object is made of, never what it is doing. <code>--decay</code> and
            <code>--bleed</code> are relative and scale with the object; the hairline is
            absolute and does not. Below 80px the decay band has no room to resolve, so
            switch to ceramic rather than continuing to compress it.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--3">
          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <h3>.lit</h3>
            <p class="cer-text">The default. Four layers: black bleed, hairline, hard contact light, soft inward decay. Everything rectangular that is not an input.</p>
            <pre class="ds-code">{`--lift: 0.19;
--bleed: 12px;
--decay: 15px;
background: var(--s2);`}</pre>
          </div>
          <div class="cer-card lit lit--ceramic">
            <h3>.lit--ceramic</h3>
            <p class="cer-text">Decay zero. No interior information at all — the purest form of the thesis, the cheapest to draw, and the only preset that cannot band.</p>
            <pre class="ds-code">{`--lift: 0.26;
--bleed: 16px;
/* no decay layer */`}</pre>
          </div>
          <div class="cer-card lit lit--sunk">
            <h3>.lit--sunk</h3>
            <p class="cer-text">The pair inverted. One flip supplies the entire input vocabulary: field wells, toggle tracks, progress channels, log panels, pressed buttons.</p>
            <pre class="ds-code">{`background: var(--s1);
inset (dark) · inside
inset (light) · outside`}</pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cer-card lit ds-note">
          <div class="ds-rule">
            <span class="n">↕</span>
            <p><b>Scale rule</b>decay ≈ 0.07 × min(w, h) · bleed ≈ 0.06 × min(w, h) · lift = clamp(0.19 + 0.14 × (1 − size/200), 0.19, 0.34). Small objects get a shorter, brighter band.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ds-rule">
            <span class="n">◫</span>
            <p><b>Dither is not optional polish</b>A gradient from #000 to #14151a crosses about twenty 8-bit levels over hundreds of pixels; untreated, <code>.lit</code> shows concentric rings on OLED. This page carries one fixed <code>feTurbulence</code> overlay at 2.8%, and the WebGL ring dithers in-shader at ±0.5/255.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================== 4 · STATUS =========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-status">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§5 · THE STATUS PRIMITIVE</p>
          <h2 id="ds-status" class="cer-h2">State light is omnidirectional and tinted</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            <code>inset 0 0 0 1.5px</code> — no offset, no blur. A complete, even ring is
            something no light position could ever produce, which is precisely why hue can
            never be misread as lighting (I5). Status is a token, not a component, so the
            same signal works at a 6px dot and a 116px disc with no second implementation.
            Note that <code>--lift</code> is 0.42 here against 0.19 for neutral: that is
            matched <em>luminance</em>, not matched alpha.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div id="ds-status-demo">
          <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--4">
            {statuses.map((s) => (
              <div class="cer-card lit ds-stack">
                <div class="ds-row" style="gap: 12px">
                  <div class={`cer-disc lit--status is-${s.key}`} style="width: 62px; height: 62px">
                    <div>
                      <div class="v">{s.v}</div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <p class="cer-ui">{s.label}</p>
                    <p class="cer-mono" style="font-size: 11px">{s.rgb}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ds-row" style="gap: 9px">
                  <span class={`cer-badge lit--status is-${s.key}`}>
                    <i class="cer-dot"></i>{s.label}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <p class="cer-mono" style="font-size: 11px">.is-{s.key} · {s.note}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
            <div class="cer-card lit ds-stack">
              <p class="cer-eyebrow">I8 · greyscale audit</p>
              <p class="cer-text" style="font-size: 12.5px">
                The deuteranopic separation between the amber and the red at this luminance
                is thinner than it looks in a swatch. Every ring is therefore paired with a
                dot, a word, or both — desaturate the row above and nothing is lost.
              </p>
              <button id="ds-grey" class="cer-pill lit" type="button" aria-pressed="false">
                <svg class="icon icon--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-filter" /></svg>
                Desaturate
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================== 5 · LIGHT =========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-light">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§6 · LIGHT MODEL</p>
          <h2 id="ds-light" class="cer-h2">Fixed rest, impulse on action, asleep between</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            One global vector, unit length, written by one rAF spring into
            <code>--lx</code> / <code>--ly</code>. It does <em>not</em> track the pointer:
            move your cursor across this page without clicking and nothing changes at all.
            Press any control and the light takes an impulse toward that element, then
            springs back to rest — motion is evidence that something happened (I7). When
            the spring settles the loop cancels itself, so the page costs zero scripting
            between interactions.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-split">
          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <div class="ds-row" style="gap: 22px">
              <div class="ds-vector lit lit--sunk" aria-hidden="true">
                <i id="ds-vec"></i>
                <u></u>
              </div>
              <div class="ds-monitor ds-ring-meta">
                <p class="cer-eyebrow">Reference monitor · live</p>
                <p class="cer-mono">--lx <b id="ds-mon-lx">-0.220</b> · --ly <b id="ds-mon-ly">-0.975</b></p>
                <p class="cer-mono">rest <b id="ds-mon-rest">347°</b> · stiff <b>0.14</b> · damp <b>0.76</b></p>
                <p class="cer-mono">frames <b id="ds-mon-frames">0</b> · loop <b id="ds-mon-loop">asleep</b></p>
                <p class="cer-text ds-note" style="font-size: 12.5px">
                  Every shadow on the page is a <code>calc()</code> of these two numbers.
                  No element is ever touched by JavaScript.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Impulse sources</p>
            <div class="ds-row ds-note">
              <button class="cer-pill lit" type="button">Press me</button>
              <button class="cer-pill lit" type="button">And me</button>
            </div>
            <p class="cer-text ds-note" style="font-size: 12.5px">
              <code>pointerdown</code> on a control injects velocity toward that
              element's screen position at gain 0.055; <code>focusin</code> does the same
              at 0.03, so keyboard navigation lights the page exactly like a click.
              Settling takes about 400ms with one small overshoot.
            </p>
            <pre class="ds-code">{`const FIXED = { x: -0.22, y: 0.97 };
const STIFF = 0.14, DAMP = 0.76;

light.vx += (FIXED.x - light.x) * STIFF;
light.vx *= DAMP;
light.x  += light.vx;`}</pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================ 6 · RING =========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-ring-h">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§7 · THE CONFORMAL RING</p>
          <h2 id="ds-ring-h" class="cer-h2">One Möbius map, no easing function anywhere</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            The single WebGL surface on the page. Its falloff field is warped by a disc
            automorphism, <code>w = (z − a) / (1 − āz)</code>, which maps the unit disc to
            itself and fixes the boundary. The silhouette therefore stays a
            mathematically exact circle while the interior level sets are pushed
            off-centre, and a constant-width band in <code>w</code>-space becomes a
            variable-width band on screen: calligraphic line weight, free. Taking the arc
            angle in <code>w</code>-space rather than <code>z</code>-space makes the
            progress head accelerate and decelerate around the ring with no hand-authored
            easing at all. <code>a</code> is a single complex number — it is the light
            vector.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-split">
          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <h3>Release</h3>
            <p class="cer-text" style="margin-bottom: 16px">api-gateway · main</p>
            <div class="ds-ring-wrap">
              <canvas
                id="ds-ring" class="cer-ring" width="232" height="232"
                style="width: 116px; height: 116px" aria-hidden="true"
              ></canvas>
              <div class="ds-ring-meta">
                <div class="sha">3d10bb4</div>
                <div class="msg">Batch ingest writes, drop per-row commit</div>
                <div style="margin-top: 11px">
                  <span id="ds-ring-badge" class="cer-badge lit--status is-idle"><i class="cer-dot"></i>ready</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cer-bar lit lit--sunk is-info" style="margin-top: 18px">
              <i id="ds-ring-bar" style="width: 0%"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-row" style="margin-top: 16px; gap: 10px">
              <button class="cer-pill lit" type="button" data-ring="run">Run determinate</button>
              <button class="cer-pill lit" type="button" data-ring="indeterminate">Indeterminate</button>
              <button class="cer-pill lit--status is-danger" type="button" data-ring="fail">Fail</button>
              <button class="cer-pill cer-pill--ghost" type="button" data-ring="reset">Reset</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Drive modes</p>
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">01</span>
              <p><b>Still</b><code>a = 0</code>, arc off. Terminal states stop dead and switch to a still tinted ring, so motion unambiguously means “in progress”.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">02</span>
              <p><b>Indeterminate</b><code>a = 0.7·(cos ωt, sin ωt)</code>. The band thickens and thins as the map compresses and expands it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">03</span>
              <p><b>Determinate</b><code>a</code> follows the arc head; progress is the fraction. Watch the head slow at the top of the circle and quicken at the bottom.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="cer-text ds-note" style="font-size: 12.5px">
              At most one WebGL context per page — context limits are real and mobile
              browsers drop contexts on backgrounding. This canvas handles
              <code>webglcontextlost</code> by remounting, caps its backing store at 2×
              DPR, and degrades to a static CSS ring carrying the same hairline if a
              context cannot be obtained. The loader is the only component in the system
              permitted to animate without a user action, because ongoing work is itself
              the event.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================= 7 · COMPONENTS ======================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-components">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§8 · COMPONENTS</p>
          <h2 id="ds-components" class="cer-h2">Geometry is normative</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            Every component is one of the four presets plus layout. There are no bespoke
            shadows below this line. A button press inverts the pair rather than moving
            the button, so a press can never cause layout shift; focus takes a tinted
            omnidirectional ring, because white contact light at 0.16 over
            <code>--s2</code> cannot clear WCAG 2.4.11's 3:1 and the tinted ring can.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--2">
          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Controls</p>
            <div class="ds-row ds-note" style="gap: 12px">
              <button class="cer-pill lit" type="button">
                <svg class="icon icon--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-refresh" /></svg>Re-run
              </button>
              <button class="cer-pill cer-pill--ghost" type="button">
                <svg class="icon icon--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-download" /></svg>Export
              </button>
              <button class="cer-pill lit" type="button" disabled>Disabled</button>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-row ds-note" style="gap: 12px; margin-top: 16px">
              <input class="cer-field lit lit--sunk" placeholder="Filter services…" aria-label="Filter services" />
              <button
                class="cer-toggle lit lit--sunk" type="button"
                aria-checked="true" role="switch" aria-label="Auto-rollback"
              ><span></span></button>
              <button
                class="cer-toggle lit lit--sunk" type="button"
                aria-checked="false" role="switch" aria-label="Require approval"
              ><span></span></button>
            </div>
            <p class="cer-mono ds-note" style="font-size: 11px">
              pill 37 × r19 · field 37 × r10 · toggle 46 × 27, travel 3.5 → 22.5
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Knobs · thresholds</p>
            <div class="ds-row ds-note" style="gap: 26px; margin-top: 14px">
              <div class="ds-spec">
                <div class="cer-knob lit--status is-warning"><i style="transform: rotate(48deg)"></i></div>
                <p class="ds-cap">Error budget · 68%</p>
              </div>
              <div class="ds-spec">
                <div class="cer-knob lit"><i style="transform: rotate(-14deg)"></i></div>
                <p class="ds-cap">CPU target · 45%</p>
              </div>
              <div class="ds-spec">
                <div class="cer-knob lit"><i style="transform: rotate(87deg)"></i></div>
                <p class="ds-cap">Scale ceiling · 82%</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="cer-mono ds-note" style="font-size: 11px">
              78px · indicator 2 × 15px in --edge, so it reads as a cut
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Rows · discs · avatars</p>
            <div class="ds-stack ds-note" style="margin-top: 12px">
              <div class="cer-row lit is-interactive">
                <span class="cer-dot" style="--glow: var(--hue-success)"></span>
                <div class="name">api-gateway<small>us-east-1 · 12 tasks</small></div>
                <div class="num">42ms</div>
                <span class="cer-badge lit--status is-success">healthy</span>
              </div>
              <div class="cer-row lit is-interactive">
                <span class="cer-dot" style="--glow: var(--hue-warning)"></span>
                <div class="name">ingest<small>us-west-2 · 24 tasks</small></div>
                <div class="num">840ms</div>
                <span class="cer-badge lit--status is-warning">degraded</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-row" style="margin-top: 16px; gap: 18px">
              <div class="cer-disc lit--status is-success" style="width: 78px; height: 78px">
                <div><div class="v">99.94%</div><div class="k">UPTIME</div></div>
              </div>
              <div class="cer-disc lit lit--ceramic" style="width: 78px; height: 78px">
                <div><div class="v">4.2k</div><div class="k">RPS</div></div>
              </div>
              <div class="cer-avatar lit lit--ceramic">ES</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Well · machine text</p>
            <div class="cer-log lit lit--sunk ds-note" style="margin-top: 12px">
              {activity.map(([t, cls, msg]) => (
                <div><time>{t}</time><span class={cls}>{msg}</span></div>
              ))}
            </div>
            <p class="cer-eyebrow" style="margin-top: 18px">Nav rail · ≤720px projection</p>
            <div class="ds-rail lit lit--sunk ds-note" style="margin-top: 10px">
              <button class="ds-chip" aria-current="true" type="button">Overview</button>
              <button class="ds-chip" type="button" style="--glow: var(--hue-warning)">
                Services<span class="tick"></span>
              </button>
              <button class="ds-chip" type="button">Deploys</button>
              <button class="ds-chip" type="button">Settings</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================== 8 · ICONS =========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-icons">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§8.1 · ICONS &amp; BREADCRUMBS</p>
          <h2 id="ds-icons" class="cer-h2">An icon is an incision, not a drawing</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            The path is absolute black — the same ink as the hairline — and it carries the
            same asymmetric pair: dark line, light edge offset opposite the light vector.
            That is what makes it read as cut into the surface rather than printed on it.
            <code>vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke</code> holds the weight at 1.5px from
            14px to 40px, exactly as the hairline never scales with its element.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-split">
          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <div class="ds-row" style="gap: 26px">
              <div class="ds-spec">
                <div class="cer-glyph lit lit--sunk" style="width: 66px; height: 66px; border-radius: 18px">
                  <svg class="icon icon--xl" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-target" /></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="ds-cap">incised — default</p>
              </div>
              <div class="ds-spec">
                <div class="cer-glyph lit" style="width: 66px; height: 66px; border-radius: 18px">
                  <svg class="icon icon--xl icon--raised" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-target" /></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="ds-cap">raised — sign flipped</p>
              </div>
              <div class="ds-spec">
                <div class="cer-glyph lit lit--ceramic" style="width: 66px; height: 66px; border-radius: 18px">
                  <svg class="icon icon--xl" style="--icon-lift: 0" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-target" /></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="ds-cap">flat — no pair</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-row" style="gap: 30px; margin-top: 22px">
              <div class="ds-spec"><svg class="icon icon--xs" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg><span class="ds-cap">14 · inline</span></div>
              <div class="ds-spec"><svg class="icon icon--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg><span class="ds-cap">16 · dense</span></div>
              <div class="ds-spec"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg><span class="ds-cap">20 · default</span></div>
              <div class="ds-spec"><svg class="icon icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg><span class="ds-cap">24 · touch</span></div>
              <div class="ds-spec"><svg class="icon icon--xl" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock" /></svg><span class="ds-cap">40 · feature</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">01</span>
              <p><b>24 × 24 grid, 2px safe margin</b>Live area is 20 × 20. Nothing touches the frame.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">02</span>
              <p><b>Stroke only, no fills</b>A filled shape is a surface, and surfaces get the depth primitive. Icons are lines.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">03</span>
              <p><b>Angles at 0°, 45°, 90° only</b>Arcs otherwise. Arbitrary diagonals break the family faster than any other rule.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">04</span>
              <p><b>Icons never take hue</b>Status is the ring. An icon may sit inside a tinted chip; it never becomes the tint.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ds-rule">
              <span class="n">05</span>
              <p><b>Never load-bearing alone</b>Every icon in a nav or a control has a text label beside it. The set is a scanning aid, not a vocabulary.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ds-set" style="margin-top: 14px">
          {iconSet.map((name) => (
            <div class="ds-cell lit">
              <svg class="icon icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"><use href={`#i-${name}`} /></svg>
              <span class="nm">{name}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--2" style="margin-top: 14px">
          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Breadcrumb · desktop projection</p>
            <nav class="cer-crumbs ds-note" aria-label="Example breadcrumb" style="margin-top: 12px">
              <a>Pursue</a>
              <svg class="icon icon--xs icon--mark" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron-right" /></svg>
              <a>Discover</a>
              <svg class="icon icon--xs icon--mark" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron-right" /></svg>
              <span aria-current="page">IT Support Services BPA</span>
            </nav>
            <p class="cer-text ds-note" style="font-size: 12.5px; margin-top: 12px">
              Ancestors dim, current node bright and never a link. The separator is a
              <code>.icon--mark</code>: a dim stroke, not a cut, because a separator is
              not an object and does not get the light treatment.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="cer-card lit">
            <p class="cer-eyebrow">Breadcrumb · mobile projection</p>
            <div class="ds-note" style="margin-top: 12px">
              <button class="cer-crumb-back lit lit--ceramic" type="button">
                <svg class="icon icon--xs" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron-left" /></svg>Discover
              </button>
              <p class="cer-display" style="font-size: 19px; margin-top: 12px">IT Support Services BPA</p>
            </div>
            <p class="cer-text ds-note" style="font-size: 12.5px; margin-top: 12px">
              The back control <em>names</em> the parent — never a bare chevron — so the
              hierarchy stays legible with only one node visible. Item names truncate;
              ancestors never do.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================ 9 · TYPE =========================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-type-h">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§9 · TYPE</p>
          <h2 id="ds-type-h" class="cer-h2">Four roles, and a display face that blooms</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            Heavy display type blooms on near-black, so the display role gets its own,
            dimmer ink (<code>--ink-display</code>) and a hard floor at 16px, below which
            the face loses its shape. Supporting prose runs at 300 weight and never sits
            on <code>--ink-3</code> — thin strokes vanish against low-contrast surfaces.
            Every value that updates in place takes tabular figures, because proportional
            digits jitter horizontally and that reads as flicker here.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="cer-card lit ds-type">
          <div>
            <span class="meta">display · Rammetto One 400 · ≥16px · --ink-display · tracking −0.015em</span>
            <p class="cer-display" style="font-size: 32px">Boundary</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="meta">ui · Cabin 400/500/600 · anything you click, label or scan</span>
            <p class="cer-ui" style="font-size: 15px">Deploy to production · Require approval · 6 services across 3 regions</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="meta">text · Titillium Web 300 · ≥12px · supporting prose</span>
            <p class="cer-text">The fill is one value edge to edge; all the signal is at the boundary.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="meta">mono · machine text only: SHAs, timestamps, log lines</span>
            <p class="cer-mono">3d10bb4 · 14:22:07Z · p95 840ms · --lift 0.42</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ======================= 10 · ANTI-PATTERNS ====================== -->
      <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-anti">
        <header>
          <p class="cer-eyebrow">§12 · ANTI-PATTERNS</p>
          <h2 id="ds-anti" class="cer-h2">The failures that collapse it into a generic dark theme</h2>
          <p class="cer-text">
            These are what implementing from a description rather than from the rules
            produces. Each one is individually reasonable and collectively fatal.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="cer-card lit">
          {antiPatterns.map(([dont, why]) => (
            <div class="ds-anti">
              <svg class="icon icon--sm x" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-close" /></svg>
              <p><b>{dont}</b><span>{why}</span></p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="ds-footer">
      <p>
        CERAMIC v1.0 · single mode · tokens:
        <a href="/ceramic/ceramic.tokens.json">ceramic.tokens.json</a> · layer:
        <a href="/ceramic/ceramic.css">ceramic.css</a> · sibling system:
        <a href="/design/prismatic">PRISM</a>
      </p>

      <ul class="ds-check lit lit--sunk">
        {acceptance.map((line) => (
          <li>
            <svg class="icon icon--xs" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check" /></svg>
            <span>{line}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </footer>

    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        'use strict';

        var root = document.documentElement;
        var reduced = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

        /* =============================================================
           LIGHT — fixed rest, impulse on action, sleeps when settled.
           This loop is the only thing that writes --lx / --ly, and it
           is the only rAF on the page. It also drives the ring, so the
           page never has two clocks.
        ============================================================= */

        var FIXED = { x: -0.22, y: 0.97 }; // y-up; --ly is written negated
        var STIFF = 0.14;
        var DAMP = 0.76;

        var light = { x: FIXED.x, y: FIXED.y, vx: 0, vy: 0 };
        var running = false;
        var last = 0;
        var frames = 0;

        var el = {
          lx: document.getElementById('ds-lx'),
          ly: document.getElementById('ds-ly'),
          loop: document.getElementById('ds-loop'),
          monLx: document.getElementById('ds-mon-lx'),
          monLy: document.getElementById('ds-mon-ly'),
          monRest: document.getElementById('ds-mon-rest'),
          monFrames: document.getElementById('ds-mon-frames'),
          monLoop: document.getElementById('ds-mon-loop'),
          vec: document.getElementById('ds-vec'),
        };

        function writeLight() {
          var m = Math.hypot(light.x, light.y) || 1;
          var lx = (light.x / m).toFixed(3);
          var ly = (-light.y / m).toFixed(3);
          root.style.setProperty('--lx', lx);
          root.style.setProperty('--ly', ly);
          el.lx.textContent = lx;
          el.ly.textContent = ly;
          el.monLx.textContent = lx;
          el.monLy.textContent = ly;
          /* the monitor needle points AT the light source */
          el.vec.style.transform = 'rotate(' + (Math.atan2(light.x, light.y) * 180) / Math.PI + 'deg)';
        }

        function setLoopState(on) {
          var word = on ? 'running' : 'asleep';
          el.loop.textContent = word;
          el.monLoop.textContent = word;
        }

        function wake() {
          if (reduced || running) return;
          running = true;
          setLoopState(true);
          last = performance.now();
          requestAnimationFrame(frame);
        }

        function nudge(node, gain) {
          if (reduced) return;
          var r = node.getBoundingClientRect();
          var x = ((r.left + r.width / 2) / innerWidth) * 2 - 1;
          var y = -(((r.top + r.height / 2) / innerHeight) * 2 - 1);
          light.vx += x * (gain || 0.055);
          light.vy += y * (gain || 0.055);
          wake();
        }

        document.addEventListener('pointerdown', function (e) {
          var node = e.target.closest('button, input, a, .cer-row, .cer-knob, .cer-card, .cer-disc');
          if (node) nudge(node);
        });

        document.addEventListener('focusin', function (e) {
          if (e.target.matches('input, button, a')) nudge(e.target, 0.03);
        });

        /* =============================================================
           RING — the one WebGL surface on the page.
        ============================================================= */

        var VERT =
          'attribute vec2 p; varying vec2 vUv;' +
          'void main() { vUv = p; gl_Position = vec4(p, 0.0, 1.0); }';

        var FRAG = [
          '#extension GL_OES_standard_derivatives : enable',
          'precision highp float;',
          'varying vec2 vUv;',
          'uniform vec2 uA;',
          'uniform vec3 uHue;',
          'uniform float uLine;',
          'uniform float uLift;',
          'uniform float uDecay;',
          'uniform float uProgress;',
          'uniform float uArc;',
          'vec2 cmul(vec2 a, vec2 b) { return vec2(a.x * b.x - a.y * b.y, a.x * b.y + a.y * b.x); }',
          'vec2 cdiv(vec2 a, vec2 b) { float d = dot(b, b); return vec2(dot(a, b), a.y * b.x - a.x * b.y) / d; }',
          'vec2 mobius(vec2 z, vec2 a) { return cdiv(z - a, vec2(1.0, 0.0) - cmul(vec2(a.x, -a.y), z)); }',
          'float hash(vec2 v) { return fract(sin(dot(v, vec2(12.9898, 78.233))) * 43758.5453); }',
          'void main() {',
          '  vec2 z = vUv / 0.86;',
          '  vec2 wv = mobius(z, uA);',
          '  float d = length(wv);',
          '  float px = max(fwidth(d), 1e-5);',
          '  float ang = atan(wv.y, wv.x);',
          '  float t = mod(1.5707963 - ang, 6.2831853) / 6.2831853;',
          '  float mask = 1.0;',
          '  if (uArc > 0.5) {',
          '    float e = max(fwidth(t) * 1.5, 0.002);',
          '    mask = 1.0 - smoothstep(uProgress - e, uProgress + e, t);',
          '  }',
          '  float line = (1.0 - smoothstep(0.0, px * uLine, abs(d - 1.0))) * mask;',
          '  float inside = 1.0 - smoothstep(1.0 - px, 1.0 + px, d);',
          '  float under = smoothstep(1.16, 1.0, d) * step(1.0, d);',
          /* The lift is a RIM, brightest against the hairline and falling
             inward — the shader form of the CSS contact light. band 0.03 is
             the ceramic rim; a wider band is the .lit decay. Keeping it a rim
             is what lets a colour picker read the same #1c1e26 at the centre
             of this ring as at the centre of every CSS disc on the page. */
          '  float band = uDecay < 0.001 ? 0.03 : uDecay;',
          '  float lift = smoothstep(1.0 - band, 1.0, d) * step(d, 1.0);',
          '  vec3 surface = vec3(0.063, 0.067, 0.094);',
          '  vec3 fill = vec3(0.110, 0.118, 0.149);',
          '  vec3 col = mix(surface, surface * 0.24, under);',
          '  col = mix(col, fill, inside);',
          '  col += lift * uLift * mask * uHue;',
          '  col = mix(col, vec3(0.0), line);',
          '  col += (hash(gl_FragCoord.xy) - 0.5) / 255.0;',
          '  gl_FragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);',
          '}',
        ].join('\n');

        var HUES = {
          neutral: [1, 1, 1],
          success: [0.478, 0.839, 0.627],
          warning: [0.925, 0.761, 0.416],
          danger: [0.941, 0.541, 0.502],
          info: [0.541, 0.706, 0.941],
        };

        /* state: idle | running | indeterminate | done | failed */
        var job = { state: 'idle', progress: 0, phase: 0 };
        var ring = null;

        function compile(gl, type, src) {
          var s = gl.createShader(type);
          gl.shaderSource(s, src);
          gl.compileShader(s);
          if (!gl.getShaderParameter(s, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(s));
          return s;
        }

        function mountRing() {
          ring = null;
          var canvas = document.getElementById('ds-ring');
          if (!canvas) return;

          var dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
          var cssW = canvas.clientWidth || 116;
          canvas.width = Math.round(cssW * dpr);
          canvas.height = Math.round(cssW * dpr);

          var gl = null;
          try {
            gl = canvas.getContext('webgl', { antialias: true, powerPreference: 'low-power' });
          } catch (err) {
            gl = null;
          }

          if (!gl) {
            var div = document.createElement('div');
            div.className = 'cer-ring-fallback';
            div.style.width = cssW + 'px';
            div.style.height = cssW + 'px';
            div.style.setProperty('--glow', 'var(--hue-info)');
            canvas.replaceWith(div);
            return;
          }

          canvas.addEventListener('webglcontextlost', function (e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            mountRing();
          });

          gl.getExtension('OES_standard_derivatives');
          var prog = gl.createProgram();
          gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl, gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERT));
          gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl, gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAG));
          gl.linkProgram(prog);
          gl.useProgram(prog);

          var buf = gl.createBuffer();
          gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buf);
          gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);
          var loc = gl.getAttribLocation(prog, 'p');
          gl.enableVertexAttribArray(loc);
          gl.vertexAttribPointer(loc, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);

          var u = {};
          ['uA', 'uHue', 'uLine', 'uLift', 'uDecay', 'uProgress', 'uArc'].forEach(function (n) {
            u[n] = gl.getUniformLocation(prog, n);
          });

          ring = { gl: gl, canvas: canvas, prog: prog, buf: buf, loc: loc, u: u };
          drawRing();
        }

        function drawRing() {
          if (!ring) return;
          var gl = ring.gl;
          var u = ring.u;
          gl.useProgram(ring.prog);
          gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, ring.buf);
          gl.vertexAttribPointer(ring.loc, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);
          gl.viewport(0, 0, ring.canvas.width, ring.canvas.height);

          if (job.state === 'running') {
            /* determinate: a follows the arc head */
            var a = Math.PI / 2 - job.progress * Math.PI * 2;
            gl.uniform2f(u.uA, Math.cos(a) * 0.7, Math.sin(a) * 0.7);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uProgress, job.progress);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uArc, 1);
            gl.uniform3fv(u.uHue, HUES.info);
            /* 0.42 is the status --lift: tinted light reads dimmer than white
               at equal alpha, so it is matched by luminance, not by number. */
            gl.uniform1f(u.uLift, 0.42);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uDecay, 0.14);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uLine, 2);
          } else if (job.state === 'indeterminate') {
            gl.uniform2f(u.uA, Math.cos(job.phase) * 0.7, Math.sin(job.phase) * 0.7);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uProgress, 1);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uArc, 0);
            gl.uniform3fv(u.uHue, HUES.info);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uLift, 0.42);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uDecay, 0.14);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uLine, 2);
          } else {
            var hue =
              job.state === 'failed' ? HUES.danger : job.state === 'done' ? HUES.success : HUES.neutral;
            gl.uniform2f(u.uA, 0, 0);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uProgress, 1);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uArc, 0);
            gl.uniform3fv(u.uHue, hue);
            /* still + neutral is the ceramic rim (0.26); still + tinted is a
               terminal status ring (0.42). Same two numbers as the CSS. */
            gl.uniform1f(u.uLift, job.state === 'idle' ? 0.26 : 0.42);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uDecay, 0);
            gl.uniform1f(u.uLine, 1.6);
          }

          gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);
        }

        var badgeEl = document.getElementById('ds-ring-badge');
        var barEl = document.getElementById('ds-ring-bar');
        var barTrack = barEl ? barEl.parentElement : null;

        var BADGE = {
          idle: ['is-idle', 'ready'],
          running: ['is-info', 'rolling out'],
          indeterminate: ['is-info', 'working'],
          done: ['is-success', 'live'],
          failed: ['is-danger', 'rolled back'],
        };

        function paintJob() {
          var meta = BADGE[job.state];
          var pct = Math.round(job.progress * 100);
          badgeEl.className = 'cer-badge lit--status ' + meta[0];
          badgeEl.innerHTML =
            '<i class="cer-dot"></i>' + meta[1] + (job.state === 'running' ? ' ' + pct + '%' : '');
          barTrack.className =
            'cer-bar lit lit--sunk is-' +
            (job.state === 'done' ? 'success' : job.state === 'failed' ? 'danger' : 'info');
          barEl.style.width =
            (job.state === 'idle' ? 0 : job.state === 'running' ? pct : job.state === 'indeterminate' ? 0 : 100) + '%';
        }

        document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
          var btn = e.target.closest('[data-ring]');
          if (!btn) return;
          var act = btn.getAttribute('data-ring');
          if (act === 'run') {
            job.state = 'running';
            job.progress = 0;
          } else if (act === 'indeterminate') {
            job.state = 'indeterminate';
            job.progress = 0;
          } else if (act === 'fail') {
            job.state = 'failed';
            job.progress = 1;
          } else {
            job.state = 'idle';
            job.progress = 0;
          }
          paintJob();
          drawRing();
          /* reduced motion: terminal frames only, never a loop */
          if (reduced && (job.state === 'running' || job.state === 'indeterminate')) {
            job.state = 'done';
            job.progress = 1;
            paintJob();
            drawRing();
            return;
          }
          wake();
        });

        /* =============================================================
           LOOP — one clock for the spring and the ring.
        ============================================================= */

        function frame(now) {
          var dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.05);
          last = now;
          frames++;

          light.vx += (FIXED.x - light.x) * STIFF;
          light.vy += (FIXED.y - light.y) * STIFF;
          light.vx *= DAMP;
          light.vy *= DAMP;
          light.x += light.vx;
          light.y += light.vy;
          writeLight();
          el.monFrames.textContent = String(frames);

          var busy = job.state === 'running' || job.state === 'indeterminate';
          if (job.state === 'running') {
            job.progress += dt * 0.3;
            if (job.progress >= 1) {
              job.progress = 1;
              job.state = 'done';
              busy = false;
            }
            paintJob();
          } else if (job.state === 'indeterminate') {
            job.phase += dt * 2.2;
          }

          drawRing();

          var settled =
            Math.hypot(light.x - FIXED.x, light.y - FIXED.y) < 0.002 &&
            Math.hypot(light.vx, light.vy) < 0.002;

          if (settled && !busy) {
            light.x = FIXED.x;
            light.y = FIXED.y;
            light.vx = light.vy = 0;
            writeLight();
            drawRing();
            running = false;
            setLoopState(false);
            return;
          }

          requestAnimationFrame(frame);
        }

        /* =============================================================
           SHOWCASE CONTROLS
        ============================================================= */

        /* Light azimuth: degrees clockwise from overhead. Moving the rest
           position is an explicit action, so the spring travels to it. */
        var azimuth = document.getElementById('ds-azimuth');
        azimuth.addEventListener('input', function (e) {
          var deg = parseInt(e.target.value, 10);
          var rad = (deg * Math.PI) / 180;
          FIXED.x = Math.sin(rad);
          FIXED.y = Math.cos(rad);
          el.monRest.textContent = deg + '°';
          if (reduced) {
            light.x = FIXED.x;
            light.y = FIXED.y;
            writeLight();
          } else {
            wake();
          }
        });

        /* Strip the pair — leaves the hairline and the flat fill alone. */
        var strip = document.getElementById('ds-strip');
        strip.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var on = document.body.classList.toggle('ds-stripped');
          strip.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
          strip.textContent = on ? 'Restore the pair' : 'Strip the pair';
        });

        /* Greyscale audit (I8). */
        var grey = document.getElementById('ds-grey');
        var greyHost = document.getElementById('ds-status-demo');
        grey.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var on = greyHost.classList.toggle('ds-greyscale');
          grey.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
        });

        /* Toggles are buttons with aria-checked; they carry a label. */
        document.querySelectorAll('.cer-toggle').forEach(function (t) {
          t.addEventListener('click', function () {
            t.setAttribute('aria-checked', t.getAttribute('aria-checked') === 'true' ? 'false' : 'true');
          });
        });

        /* =============================================================
           BOOT
        ============================================================= */

        var resizeTimer = null;
        addEventListener('resize', function () {
          clearTimeout(resizeTimer);
          resizeTimer = setTimeout(mountRing, 180);
        });

        writeLight();
        setLoopState(false);
        paintJob();
        mountRing();
        if (document.fonts) document.fonts.ready.then(function () { mountRing(); });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
